<Layout title="An internet with room for everyone"><section class="shell py-14"><article class="max-w-2xl"><span class="eyebrow">Small by design. Open by nature.</span><h1 class="serif text-5xl mt-4 mb-7">Good work needs<br/>a little breathing room.</h1><div class="prose-copy">Feedme is an open-source home for the things people make and the lives behind them. A project, a practice, a rent payment, a wild idea. You choose where a little support would make a difference.

There are no all-or-nothing campaigns. Support is a tip and a vote of encouragement, never a promise of delivery or ownership. Creators keep tips regardless of whether they reach an aspiration.

Your identity comes from AT Protocol. Public projects live on the open social web. Private support records use Habitat’s permissioned spaces. Payments happen on Stripe’s hosted checkout.

This first release focuses on individuals and one-time support. Recurring memberships, organization roles, and discovery across independent instances are next steps.</div><div class="panel mt-8"><h2 class="section-title mb-3">A small home you can own.</h2><p class="muted text-sm">Built with TypeScript, Astro, Tailwind, and ordinary HTML. Self-host with Node or Docker on a VPS or Railway. No React runtime, no required browser JavaScript, no platform fee added by Feedme. Stripe and hosting fees still apply.</p></div><a class="button mt-7" href="/">Explore what’s growing</a></article></section></Layout>
